</code></pre>
, while using coercion, it does not make sense to distinguish false from &quot;falsy&quot;.<p>TypeScript&#x27;s dynamic narrowing has become pretty comprehensive when it comes to this kind of issue.<p>Still, Option&lt;Boolean&gt; types are bad in most contexts I think, especially in languages like JS.<p>Instead of using boolean | undefined , I much prefer explicit defaults (parameters) or properties being declared every time (data).
